WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.156
Your class counts the money for a school trip and it is ten dollars short. Until you find out why, you write the ten dollars on a note marked unexplained. A suspense account is that note.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:25.986
When a trial balance does not agree, the difference goes into a suspense account. It goes on the side that is short. Here the debit total is two hundred short, so suspense is a debit of two hundred.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:34.559
Step one: find the difference between the two totals, and enter it on the smaller side as balance brought down.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:44.098
Step two: ignore errors that did not affect the trial balance, such as omission, commission and principle. They never touch suspense.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:55.767
Step three: write the correcting journal and take its suspense leg. If the journal credits suspense, the entry goes on the credit side, with the other account's name as the detail.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:04.311
Step four: total both sides. When every error is corrected, the totals agree and nothing is left.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:18.132
Here is a real question from June 2019. Yasin's trial balance does not balance. We must prepare the suspense account. Six marks.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:26.160
The totals are debit forty-one thousand nine hundred and seventy, and credit forty-two thousand five hundred and fifty. Six errors were found.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.595
Debit is short by five hundred and eighty, so suspense opens with a debit balance of five hundred and eighty.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:46.872
Error one: the sales day book was overcast by two hundred, so the journal debits sales and credits suspense. Error three: a payment to Raul was not posted to his account. Debit Raul, credit suspense, four hundred and fifty.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:57.181
Error four: discount received of eighty was debited to discount allowed. Both accounts need a credit of eighty, so suspense gets two debits of eighty.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:06.453
Error six: rent of four hundred and thirty was posted as three hundred and forty. Rent needs ninety more: debit rent, credit suspense ninety.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:16.016
Both sides now total seven hundred and forty. The account has cleared. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:24.993
A common mistake is opening suspense on the larger side. It always goes on the side that is short.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:32.416
Another is putting in errors that did not affect the trial balance, such as the motor repairs principle error.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:44.094
Now you try. Open the suspense account, post the corrections, and check that it clears. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:03:05.653
Credit is short by three hundred, so suspense opens as a credit. Sales needs a credit of two hundred, so suspense is debited. Lina's account needs a credit of one hundred, so suspense is debited again. Error three is principle: no suspense. Both sides total three hundred.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:14.535
Remember: open on the short side, post only the suspense legs, and check that the totals agree. Now try the practice questions.
